"systemArea.categoryMap.title" = "How the macOS storage categories map to real folders";
"systemArea.categoryMap.detail" = "What each category in the System Settings storage screen actually points at.\nWhich number you're trying to shrink decides where to look.";
"systemArea.categoryMap.consequence" = "· Developer  →  ~/Library/Developer\n  iOS DeviceSupport, simulators, DerivedData. Clearing these shrinks 'Developer' and leaves 'System Data' untouched.\n\n· Applications  →  /Applications\n  Xcode alone is 15–20GB. Only deleting apps shrinks it.\n\n· System Data  →  everything else\n  ~/Library/Application Support, ~/Library/Caches, ~/Library/Containers,\n  /Library, /private/var and local snapshots all land here.";

